00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.132
I carry a nine foot candy cane.

00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:03.965
(Santas laughing)

00:02:03.965 --> 00:02:05.280
- That's enough to keep me in snacks

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.618
for a couple of hours.

00:02:06.618 --> 00:02:07.970
(Santas all talking at once)

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:08.890
- [Santa David] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.954
- I really like that buckle, Santa.

00:02:10.954 --> 00:02:12.151
- [Santa David] That
is a beautiful buckle.

00:02:12.151 --> 00:02:14.630
- I think it sort of goes
along with my magic key.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.463
- [Santa David] That's a magic key.

00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:16.690
I've seen a bunch of them.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.250
You know, we get asked this.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.500
A lot of children live
where there's no chimney.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.700
Well, Santa has a magic key

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.804
and can walk right in the front door.

00:02:23.804 --> 00:02:25.310
(Santa Curtis ho-ho-ho's)

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.204
- [Director] What are the hardest requests

00:02:26.204 --> 00:02:28.540
you've had to hear for Christmas presents?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.720
- Actually, I've got one.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.130
I was asked if I would donate my kidney

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.400
to this young girl's aunt.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.610
I have a book I keep with prayers in it

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.950
and I wrote her name down and I told her

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.290
that I'd talk to God for her to see

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.360
if we could help get at her aunt a kidney.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.940
That was probably the hardest
one I've ever had to do.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.590
- Hmm, I think the hardest one I had

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.200
was a little girl asked for her dad.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.033
- Yeah. Oh yeah.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.091
- Yeah.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.650
- Dad was deployed to
the desert at the time.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.830
- A little child, probably
five or six years old,

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.510
and the dad was incarcerated at the time.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.270
She wanted to know if
Santa could make sure

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.473
he'd be home for Christmas.

00:03:07.473 --> 00:03:08.306
- Mmm.

00:03:08.306 --> 00:03:09.340
- [Santa Clifford] Wow.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.287
- What'd you tell her, Santa?

00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:12.960
- "Santa will see what he can do."

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:13.850
- Yes!

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.302
- [Santa David] Santa
will see what he can do.

00:03:15.302 --> 00:03:16.135
- Yeah.

00:03:16.135 --> 00:03:17.630
- Last year I had a 12 year old girl

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.430
who had just given her kidney

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.300
to her eight year old sister.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.800
That was a very touching
virtual phone call

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.730
with the grandparents there too.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.330
But the toughest for me personally

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.730
was trying to fit a unicorn into my sack.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.290
One, they don't fit.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.070
And two, they poop rainbows.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.003
No live animals in Santa's sleigh.

00:03:36.028 --> 00:03:38.290
- I had a kid who wanted a live Panda.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.903
I had to explain that it
was an endangered species.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:46.824
- [Santa Joseph] Well, you know,

00:03:46.824 --> 00:03:48.010
I'm gonna make it easy for you guys.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.480
I'm just gonna take
the last spot over here

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.330
because Santa's been losing his belly

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.760
and every year I get nasty teenagers

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.520
saying I'm the skinny Santa.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.150
So I'm voluntarily putting myself here

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.060
thanks to that keto cookie.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.326
- I think he's got the best beard.

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:04.630
(Santas laughing)

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.470
- 'Cause it's all white and snowy.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.020
- When it comes to
outfits, I have to admit,

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.860
I like yours as number one.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.210
I put you to the front of the line, sir.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.043
- I'm with that down.

00:04:13.043 --> 00:04:14.883
Come down to the front of the line.

00:04:16.153 --> 00:04:18.810
(Santas laughing)

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.400
- I think, actually, I'd accept this

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.623
just the way it is.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.303
- [Santa Clifford] All right.

00:04:23.303 --> 00:04:24.873
- That was easy.

00:04:24.873 --> 00:04:26.730
- [Santa Clifford] Consensus already?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.360
- Well, because they bring children in

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.630
and the children make the decision

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.735
in the Santa game.

00:04:30.735 --> 00:04:31.568
- They're the important ones.

00:04:31.568 --> 00:04:32.820
- [Santa Curtis] They're
the ones we gotta listen to.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.760
I think that's probably one
of the biggest qualities

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.130
of Santa is we actually
listen to the children,

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.460
hear what they're saying to us,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.810
and actually respond to 'em.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.870
- My friend, there is no greater job

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.340
in the whole world than the one we have.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.900
- I absolutely agree.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.158
Yep.

00:04:47.158 --> 00:04:51.270
(Santa Joseph ho-ho-ho's)

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.350
- I think there's kids!

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.633
- Our first child.

00:04:54.498 --> 00:04:57.780
(Santas all laughing together)

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.203
- [Santa Joseph] Merry Christmas!

00:04:59.203 --> 00:05:01.910
